  "slug": "edge-non-hermitian-4a89",
  "summary": "Recent preprints constrain and extend how gain, loss, and nonreciprocal coupling can tune non-Hermitian eigenstate structure.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of gain-loss balance and coupling asymmetry as handles on non-Hermitian spectral structure. A preprint on time-dependent non-Hermitian systems with T symmetry shows that gain-loss induced symmetry breaking is forbidden even for random gain-loss distributions, establishing a constraint on such control. A second preprint introduces pseudo-altermagnetism, in which balanced gain and loss mimic altermagnetic spin splitting, with movable nodal structures. A third shows that tunable nonreciprocal coupling near a second-order polarization exceptional point produces state-selective eigenstate splitting, with one branch distinguished. The items are heterogeneous: one establishes a constraint while the other two describe control mechanisms. What is new is the specific combination of mechanisms and constraints rather than a single unified result.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
